  {
    "Name": "Help and documentation",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Start with read-only evidence, review every proposed change, and use Activity when an operation needs verification or follow-up.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.StatusBar",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Informational icon",
    "Id": "StandardIcon",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Keyboard",
    "Id": "Title",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Press Ctrl+K to search all tasks and tools. Use Tab and arrow keys to move through navigation, tabs, tables, dialogs, and details.",
    "Id": "Message",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "1. Start with evidence",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Run Checkup first. Its four probes are read-only and report evidence coverage, not a blanket machine-health score. Open Results to inspect each command outcome before acting.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open Checkup",
    "Id": "HelpOpenCheckup",
    "Type": "ControlType.Button",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "2. Review before applying",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "A mutating command must complete a preview before WinCare issues a short-lived, single-use review receipt. The receipt is bound to the exact command, parameters, and request. Editing the parameters or replaying the receipt requires a new preview.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "If an applied command faults after mutation begins, WinCare reports that the final system state is unknown. Verify the affected resource before retrying.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "3. Use Activity for outcomes and reports",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Running work, items that need attention, completed operations, and daily reports are recorded in Activity. WinCare only promises Undo when a concrete executable compensator exists; it does not manufacture a generic rollback for commands that cannot safely provide one.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open Activity",
    "Id": "HelpOpenActivity",
    "Type": "ControlType.Button",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": false
  },
  {
    "Name": "Plugin trust",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Remote plugin installation is disabled unless the exact catalog bytes verify against a WinCare-pinned catalog signing key and the selected package includes publisher-signed manifest metadata. Capability declarations are consent metadata only: full-trust in-process plugins are not sandboxed by those declarations.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open Plugin Store",
    "Id": "HelpOpenPluginStore",
    "Type": "ControlType.Button",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Guard status",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "WinCare Guard is currently an experimental local daemon boundary, not a production SCM-installed Windows service. Its IPC pipe is local-only and explicitly access-controlled, but production service installation, per-user service authorization, and native notification integration are not claimed as complete.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Troubleshooting and logs",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open Settings to find the local WinCare data directory. Activity persistence and preference-save problems are surfaced in the app. Fatal UI faults are written under the WinCare logs directory and the process exits rather than continuing in an unknown state.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open Settings",
    "Id": "HelpOpenSettings",
    "Type": "ControlType.Button",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Open WinCare user guide on GitHub",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Hyperlink",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "Accessibility",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
  },
  {
    "Name": "WinCare uses native WinUI controls and explicit automation names for interactive controls. Windows text scaling, High Contrast, keyboard navigation, and Narrator remain first-class release checks. If a screen clips at your text or display scale, report the exact screen and scale so it can be reproduced.",
    "Id": "",
    "Type": "ControlType.Text",
    "Enabled": true,
    "Offscreen": true
